📝 EKS Setup – Short Notes
Create VPC with public/private subnets

Enable OIDC provider for the cluster

Create IAM roles for cluster, nodes, and service accounts

Create EKS cluster with VPC and IAM role

Create node groups (EC2 or Fargate)

Update kubeconfig using aws eks update-kubeconfig

Verify access with kubectl get nodes

Deploy workloads (YAML, Helm, etc.)

Use IRSA for pod-level AWS access

Enable monitoring/logging

Apply security best practices (RBAC, network policies)